.SH NAME
CSSMathClamp.CSSMathClamp \- CSSMathClamp: CSSMathClamp() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSMathClamp()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]CSSMathClamp\f[R] object representing a CSS \f[CR]clamp()\f[R]
function.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new CSSMathClamp(lower, value, upper)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]lower\f[R]
A \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] object \(en either a number or
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] \(en representing the minimum value.
.TP
\f[B]value\f[R]
A \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] object \(en either a number or
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] \(en representing the preferred value.
.TP
\f[B]upper\f[R]
A \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] object \(en either a number or
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] \(en representing the maximum value.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if there is a \f[I]failure\f[R] when adding the three arguments.
